  "_about": "Lane V64P, read by PoiseTable.cs. armour = HYPER-ARMOUR: while a fighter is inside the armoured window of one of his moves a clean hit still damages (x damageMul) but does not stagger, knock down or posture-break him and the swing goes on. Per fighter key (Dracula / Pitborn), rows in file order, first matching row wins, move = id | * | prefix pattern like heavy*, 'armour': false excludes a move. The window: Windup from tick fromTick (a heavy charge parks at its chamber tick 10, so fromTick <= 10 covers the charge) + the whole Active window + the first recoveryTicks ticks of Recovery. knockMul scales the knock-back of the hit, postureMul scales the posture it adds (an armoured fighter's posture stops below max so he can never be posture-broken inside the window). meter = POISE METER: every clean, interrupting hit on a fighter is counted, hits older than windowTicks (60 = 1 s) are forgotten; after `hits` of them the NEXT hit is absorbed: it damages (x absorbDamageMul) but does not stagger, a stagger already running is cut short (break-out) and a grace window of breakOutTicks starts in which hits damage (x graceDamageMul) but never interrupt. Anti stun-lock for both fighters. countArmoured: do armoured hits count toward the meter. fighters[] overrides any meter field per fighter (-1 = inherit, enabled false = no meter). riposte = damage multiplier on the riposte moves (applied in Duel.Resolve). enabled false or no file = the exact old rules.",
